exact integers, so wrong coordinates cannot pass.

## If one of these fails

The kernel will tell you *which chunk* and not which edge. To get the edge:

```lean
#eval deGrey.badEdges     -- every offending pair, and the squared distance it has
#eval deGrey.denomSq      -- the squared distance a real unit edge must show
```

`badEdges` runs compiled, so it is instant at any size, and an empty result is exactly
a valid certificate (`UDCert.badEdges_eq_nil_iff`).
-/

